      "credit": "\"Banganarti 2004: Inscriptions\" in \"Polish Archaeology in the Mediterranean\" 16, Fig. 1",
      "source": "Paper graffito Banganarti",
      "description": "Graffito from Banganarti in Sudan, late 13th-first half of the 14th century. It mentions Paper, a self-proclaimed \"small king\" of Dongola, who is generally assumed to be the ruler of a post-Makurian successor state. In Lajtar \"A Late Christian Pilgrimage Centre in Nubia. The Evidence of Wall Inscriptions in the Upper Church at Banganarti\" p. 135 the full inscription is translated as follows:\n\"That grace is given to us by the Archangel, the salvation of our souls. I, Paper, the Small King of the town of Toungoul, wrote (this).\"",
